This page develops conditional mathematical identities for countable and measurable canonical laws, positive trace-class Gibbs operators, finite probability models, and finite-range lattice limits. The partition-function results require the stated local summability envelopes; a lower energy bound alone does not ensure a finite countable partition sum. The operator result assumes the Axiom of Choice and a positive trace-class Gibbs operator.

The finite-range pressure theorem is restricted to finite alphabets, bounded translation-invariant interactions of finite range, and cubic boxes with free boundary. Boundary changes are covered only under the stated surface-order energy bound. Concentration and the limiting mean are asserted only at differentiability points. The transfer-matrix result is specific to the stated periodic two-state chain. No unrestricted ensemble-equivalence or general thermodynamic-limit claim is made.

The entropy, mutual-information, Bose/Fermi, and response-covariance results are statements about explicitly specified finite or countable probability laws. They make no claim that a physical preparation or measured fluctuation has been established.
